          "title": "Catch the Ten",
          "subtitle": "Trick-taking",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Catch the Ten is an eighteenth-century Scottish point-trick ace-ten game, also called Scots Whist or Scotch Whist."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Catch the Ten is recorded as an eighteenth-century Scottish point-trick game. It belongs to the ace-ten style of play and is related to Solo Whist through trump and trick control."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "2-8 players use the table arrangement described for Catch the Ten."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "36-card French-suited pack"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "36-card French-suited pack, score area, and enough table space for play."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Deal from a 36-card French pack and determine trumps for the hand."
            }
          ]
